                <pb facs="0223" n="121" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12273: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-23T16:00:00+08:00">January 23, 1933—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 23—5:58 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>78. Young Marshal left Peiping yesterday at 2 p.m., arrived Nanking 7 p.m.
                    Unconfirmed rumors here connect his visit to Nanking with presence there of Tuan
                    Chi-jui. See also Legation’s 71, January 22, 3 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
